WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.140
Venom's massive success at the box office
made a sequel virtually guaranteed.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.460
Confirmed details are all but nonexistent
at this point, but rumors and spoilers have

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.640
already started leaking — so here's a look
at what we can reasonably expect from Venom

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.140
2.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.380
If you were waiting for Woody Harrelson to
show up in Venom, then you had to wait until

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.440
the mid-credits for a brief scene.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.619
Presumably returning to his career as an investigative
journalist, Eddie Brock is summoned to San

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.680
Quentin, where Harrelson waits in a cage.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.560
Everything about the scene feels like the
foundation for a sequel, and in May 2018,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.120
Harrelson confirmed he'd be showing up in
Venom 2.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.240
If you're a Marvel Comics fan, then the hints
about Woody Harrelson's role in Venom's mid-credits

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.760
scene weren't real subtle.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:47.660
In the comics, Venom's symbiote species reproduces
asexually, and Venom's own symbiote spawn

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.600
had the horrible idea of bonding to serial
killer Cletus Kasady.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.700
The result was the villain Carnage.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.760
He's tougher than Venom and has a body count
to rival the Joker's.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.020
Even though no one in the mid-credits scene
says his name -- with Harrelson's curly red

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.909
wig, the fact that he's a convicted serial
killer, his penchant for writing in blood,

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:07.440
and of course his closing line--

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.080
"When I get outta here…and I will..."

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.579
There's gonna be carnage."

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:19.520
-- the signs point pretty hard to Venom's
bad guy having a bit more red coloring in

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.280
the second movie.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.420
Considering the nature of the character, it's
surprising Venom didn't earn an R rating.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.380
According to producer Avi Arad, Venom 2 won't
be R either.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.200
That's an even a bigger surprise with the
likelihood of Carnage's involvement in the

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:33.700
sequel.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.840
But Arad doesn't think you need an R rating
to do Carnage justice.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.620
He told Collider,

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.080
"It's not about what he does because we never
have to show the knife going from here to

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:42.580
there."

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.439
The Venom producer described Cletus Kasady
as a soul filled with torment, and that he

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.940
wants audiences to be able to feel for him.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.919
Sympathetic villains can certainly sell; the
success Tom Hiddleston found as the MCU's

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.340
Loki is proof of that.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.260
And Venom supports what Arad says about not
having to show all the violence on the screen.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.880
For example, we know Venom eats villains in
the film, though we never actually see him

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:07.380
do it.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.300
We'll see if the filmmakers can do likewise
with Carnage.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.480
But if the comics are any indication, they're
going to need to kill a lot of people off-screen

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:21.680
-- a lot.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.100
To comic book purists, divorcing Venom's movie
origin from Spider-Man may have been more

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.409
painful than a symbiote being ripped from
its host, but Venom director Ruben Fleischer

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:35.780
seems fairly sure the current live-action
versions of both characters will collide on-screen

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.280
eventually.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.680
Speaking to ScreenRant, Fleischer said,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.560
"I'd love to see [Venom] face off against
Spider-Man at some point.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.960
It feels like that's inevitable."

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.280
Fleischer went on to say he knew that both
Tom Hardy and Tom Holland were excited about

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.430
the prospect, and that he didn't know whether
or not that would mean Venom would or could

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.840
become part of the MCU.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.299
So is it possible we could we see this inevitable
clash in Venom 2?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.460
It's an enticing possibility, especially if
Carnage proves to be the sequel's villain.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.820
In the comics Spider-Man, Venom, and Carnage
have always worked as an interesting trio

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.980
of combatants, particularly with Venom sometimes
flip-flopping between allies.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.750
It's enough to make you want to imagine that
the sequel to Venom might be titled Venom:

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.940
Maximum Carnage.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.920
Considering Venom's record-breaking success,
you'd think the director could name his own

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.300
price to helm the sequel.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:28.220
But Variety pointed out that it looks like
Venom director Ruben Fleischer won't be able

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.220
to direct Venom 2, whether he wants to or
not.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:37.930
Fleischer directed 2009's post-apocalyptic
comedy Zombieland and in July 2018 Sony confirmed

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.990
the production of Zombieland 2 with pretty
much all of the original's stars returning

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.760
— as well as Fleischer, who's set to direct
the sequel.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.120
If Fleischer is going to be busy directing
Zombieland 2, then it could be difficult if

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.840
not impossible for him to also direct Venom
2.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:55.950
The Variety article didn't offer any hints
about who, if anyone, Sony might be considering

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.080
to replace Fleischer.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.659
It could be that — since both franchises
are under Sony's tent — the studio is trying

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.240
to find a way to facilitate Fleischer helming
both projects before fishing for a successor.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:11.100
Considering Harrelson will probably be playing
Carnage in Venom 2 as well as appearing in

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.080
Zombieland 2, maybe he and Fleischer could
just… carpool or something.

